# 6. Step 2 — Preview / Schema Inference

This is one of the **most important screens in the application**.

The backend receives the CSV and performs type inference.

The frontend receives something conceptually like:

```json
{
  "columns": [
    {
      "name": "name",
      "type": "STRING"
    },
    {
      "name": "age",
      "type": "INTEGER"
    },
    {
      "name": "signup_date",
      "type": "DATE"
    }
  ],
  "previewRows": [...],
  "rowCount": 12482
}
```

## Layout

```text
Create Dataset

Step 2: Review Dataset

Filename
customers.csv

12,482 rows · 8 columns
```

Then:

### Schema section

```text
Detected Schema

┌───────────────┬──────────────┬─────────────┐
│ Column        │ Detected Type│ Status      │
├───────────────┼──────────────┼─────────────┤
│ name          │ STRING       │ ✓ Valid     │
│ age           │ INTEGER      │ ✓ Valid     │
