# 17. Simple GET Query Is the Primary Experience

The frontend should make it extremely obvious that this:

```text
age > 30
AND country = US
```

becomes:

```http
GET /datasets/{id}/query?age_gt=30&country_eq=US
```

This is the **main API model** of DataServ.

The query builder is essentially a visual URL generator.

---

# 18. Advanced Query — POST Add-on

I would make this a later/secondary feature rather than designing the whole frontend around it.

Something like:

```text
Query Mode

● Simple GET
○ Advanced Query
```

Simple GET is the default.

Advanced Query could eventually support:

```text
WHERE

┌─ AND ─────────────────────────────┐
│                                   │
│ age > 30                          │
│ country = US                      │
│                                   │
│ ┌─ OR ──────────────────────────┐ │
│ │ status = active               │ │
│ │ status = pending              │ │
│ └───────────────────────────────┘ │
└───────────────────────────────────┘
```

and generate:

```http
POST /datasets/{id}/query
```

with a JSON body.

The UI can show:

```text
Generated Request

POST /datasets/123/query

{
  "where": {
    "and": [...]
  }
}
```

But this should be an **advanced escape hatch**, not the primary API.

